.TH TED 1 "November 2026" "ted 0.7.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ted \- minimal zero-dependency terminal text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ted
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ted
is a lightweight, zero-dependency terminal text editor written in C99 using raw
.BR termios (3)
input and ANSI escape sequences. If
.I FILE
is specified,
.B ted
opens it for editing; otherwise, it starts with an empty buffer and displays a centered ASCII splash banner until text is entered.
.PP
Features include C/C++ syntax highlighting, matching bracket and parenthesis highlighting, incremental search, an atomic undo/redo command stack, smart auto-indentation after opening braces, soft-tab indentation and outdentation, line duplication and cut/paste, a dynamic line-number gutter, and live terminal window resizing via
.BR SIGWINCH .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a usage summary and keybinding reference, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Output version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
Terminate option parsing. Useful when opening a file whose name begins with
.BR \- .
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.SS File & Application Control
.TP
.B Ctrl-S
Save the current buffer to disk. Prompts for a filename if the buffer has not been named yet.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Q
Quit
.BR ted .
If the buffer contains unsaved changes, pressing
.B Ctrl-Q
three times in succession is required to discard modifications and exit.
.SS Search & Navigation
.TP
.B Ctrl-F
Enter incremental search mode. Type a query to jump to matches in real time; use
.B Up / Left
and
.B Down / Right
arrow keys to cycle backward and forward through matches,
.B Enter
to confirm the jump, or
.B Esc
to cancel and restore the original cursor and scroll position.
.TP
.B Ctrl-G
Prompt for a 1-based line number and jump directly to that line, centering it vertically in the viewport.
.TP
.B Arrow Keys
Move the cursor one character or line at a time, wrapping across line boundaries at the start and end of lines.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Left / Ctrl-Right
Jump backward or forward by one word.
.TP
.B Home / End
Move the cursor to the beginning or end of the current line.
.TP
.B Page Up / Page Down
Scroll the viewport up or down by one full screen height.
.SS Editing, Indentation & History
.TP
.B Ctrl-Z
Undo the last character insertion, deletion, word deletion, line split, line join, line duplication, or line cut/paste.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Y
Redo the most recently undone edit.
.TP
.B Enter
Insert a newline, preserving the current line's leading indentation and adding an extra 4-space indent level if the line ends with
.BR { .
.TP
.B Tab
Insert spaces up to the next 4-column tab stop.
.TP
.B Shift-Tab
Outdent the current line by removing up to 4 leading spaces (or one leading tab character).
.TP
.B Ctrl-D
Duplicate the current line directly below the cursor.
.TP
.B Ctrl-K
Cut the current line into the internal clipboard and remove it from the buffer.
.TP
.B Ctrl-U
Paste the cut line from the internal clipboard directly below the current line.
.TP
.B Backspace
Delete the character before the cursor, or merge the current line onto the end of the previous line when at column 1.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Backspace / Ctrl-H
Delete the previous word (or delimiter run) before the cursor.
.TP
.B Delete
Delete the character under the cursor.
.SH SYNTAX & BRACKET HIGHLIGHTING
.B ted
automatically enables C-family syntax highlighting (keywords, preprocessor directives, primitive types, strings, character literals, numbers, and single-line or multi-line comments) when editing files ending in
.BR .c ,
.BR .h ,
or
.BR .cpp .
.PP
Whenever the cursor rests on a delimiter
.RB ( ( ", " ) ", " [ ", " ] ", " { ", or " } )
outside of strings and comments,
.B ted
highlights both the delimiter under the cursor and its matching partner in bold reverse video.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit via
.BR Ctrl-Q ,
.BR \-\-help ,
or
.BR \-\-version .
.TP
.B 1
An invalid command-line option was passed, or a fatal terminal or file I/O error occurred.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by k!M (pizslacker).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vi (1),
.BR nano (1),
.BR termios (3)